md`# brain-snapshot

A Cloud Brain recipe: once a day it fetches a list of public feeds and keeps what each one said as a public JSON file. It records. It makes no model call, ranks nothing and writes no summary: a notebook reads the files and does that.

| | |
|---|---|
| Worker | \`brain-x-snapshot\` |
| \`snapshot.run\` | procedure, the owner's own session. Fetches every source now and keeps today's files. Answers the day's index. |
| \`snapshot.sources\` | query, anyone. \`{ sources, default }\`: the list in use, and whether it is the list below. |
| \`snapshot.setSources\` | procedure, the owner's own session. \`{ sources: [...] }\` replaces the list; \`{ sources: null }\` goes back to the list below. |
| Timer | each day at the first tick after 06:00 UTC, once (\`rows\`: \`ran/<day>\`). |
| Storage | files in \`brain-static\` under \`snapshot/\`, public, tag \`snapshot\`. \`rows\`: \`sources\`, \`ran/<day>\`, \`day/<day>\`. |

## What is kept

Anyone reads these with no session. \`<day>\` is the UTC date, \`2026-10-09\`.

| Address | Holds |
|---|---|
| \`/static/snapshot/days.json\` | \`{ days: [{ day, ranAt, items }] }\`, newest first |
| \`/static/snapshot/<day>/index.json\` | \`{ day, ranAt, sources: [{ name, tier, status, count, of, bytes, ms, path, error }] }\` |
| \`/static/snapshot/<day>/<source>.json\` | \`{ source, tier, url, day, fetchedAt, count, items }\` |

An item is \`{ id, title, url, source, tier }\` and, where the feed gives them, \`points comments author published discussion summary\`. \`published\` is an ISO time. \`summary\` is text with the markup taken out, cut at 1500 characters.

- A second run on one day replaces that day's files: the last run is what is kept.
- A source that fails, or that has nothing to keep, writes no file. Its row in the index says why (\`status\`, \`error\`, \`count: 0\`), and a file an earlier run of that day made for it stays.
- Every source is fetched at the same time. Give one host one source: Reddit answered 429 to the second of two feeds, also 2 s apart (cb4, 2026-10-09), so its two subreddits are one feed.
- A failed source does not fail the run. The timer runs once a day and does not try again; \`snapshot.run\` does.
- \`of\` is how many items the feed held, \`count\` how many were kept.

## Sources

A source is a row, not code: \`{ name, tier, url, kind }\`.

- \`kind\`: \`rss\` or \`atom\` (one reader for both), or \`json\` with \`map\`, the path of each field in an item (\`"paper.id"\`), and \`items\`, the path of the list when it is not the whole answer. A \`map\` value with braces is a pattern: \`"https://huggingface.co/papers/{paper.id}"\`.
- \`tier\`: \`research\`, \`blogger\` or \`aggregator\`. Research and named writers lead. An aggregator says what people discuss.
- \`days\`: keep only items published in that many days before the run. A blog's feed holds its old posts; every \`research\` blog and every \`blogger\` here has \`days: 7\`, so most of them keep nothing on most days.
- \`keep\`: a pattern an item's text must match. arXiv's feed also lists replaced papers; \`keep\` leaves new and cross-listed ones.
- \`limit\`: at most this many items, 500 unless given.

Each source is fetched once a run, with the \`User-Agent\` \`${snapshotAgent}\`.

Measured from a Worker of cb4 on 2026-10-09 (\`tools/scratch/snapshot-probe\`): the arXiv API answered 429 "Rate exceeded" and its RSS feed 200, so the feed is used. Reddit's \`.json\` answered 403 and its \`.rss\` 200, so the feed is used, which gives no score; after about ten requests in an hour from the tests it answered 429 to each one. Anthropic and Meta AI have no feed at the addresses tried (404) and are not in the list. Gwern's feed has nothing after 2021 and is not in the list.`
// %%
viewof snapshotView = snapshotPanel({ base: client && client.base })
// %%
snapshotAgent = "lopecode-cloud-brain-snapshot/1 (+https://github.com/tomlarkworthy/lopecode)"
// %%
snapshotSources = {
  const blog = (name, url, tier = "blogger") => ({ name, tier, url, kind: "rss", days: 7 });
  return [
    { name: "arxiv", tier: "research", url: "https://rss.arxiv.org/rss/cs.AI+cs.LG+cs.CL", kind: "rss", keep: "Announce Type: (new|cross)", limit: 700 },
    { name: "hf-papers", tier: "research", url: "https://huggingface.co/api/daily_papers?limit=50", kind: "json", map: { id: "paper.id", title: "paper.title", url: "https://huggingface.co/papers/{paper.id}", points: "paper.upvotes", comments: "numComments", published: "publishedAt", summary: "paper.summary" } },
    blog("openai", "https://openai.com/news/rss.xml", "research"),
    blog("deepmind", "https://deepmind.google/blog/rss.xml", "research"),
    blog("google-research", "https://research.google/blog/rss/", "research"),
    blog("microsoft-research", "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/feed/", "research"),
    blog("bair", "https://bair.berkeley.edu/blog/feed.xml", "research"),
    blog("meta-engineering-ai", "https://engineering.fb.com/category/ai-research/feed/", "research"),
    blog("simon-willison", "https://simonwillison.net/atom/everything/"),
    blog("karpathy", "https://karpathy.bearblog.dev/feed/"),
    blog("karpathy-github", "https://karpathy.github.io/feed.xml"),
    blog("lilian-weng", "https://lilianweng.github.io/index.xml"),
    blog("sebastian-raschka", "https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/feed"),
    blog("import-ai", "https://jack-clark.net/feed/"),
    blog("eugene-yan", "https://eugeneyan.com/rss/"),
    blog("chip-huyen", "https://huyenchip.com/feed.xml"),
    blog("interconnects", "https://www.interconnects.ai/feed"),
    blog("hamel-husain", "https://hamel.dev/index.xml"),
    { name: "hn", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://hn.algolia.com/api/v1/search?tags=front_page&hitsPerPage=50", kind: "json", items: "hits", map: { id: "objectID", title: "title", url: "url", points: "points", comments: "num_comments", author: "author", published: "created_at", discussion: "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id={objectID}" } },
    { name: "reddit", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://www.reddit.com/r/MachineLearning+LocalLLaMA/top/.rss?t=day&limit=100", kind: "atom" },
    { name: "lobsters-ai", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://lobste.rs/t/ai.json", kind: "json", map: { id: "short_id", title: "title", url: "url", points: "score", comments: "comment_count", author: "submitter_user", published: "created_at", discussion: "comments_url", summary: "description_plain" } }
  ];
}
// %%
// Text of a feed field: CDATA opened, entities read, markup taken out, entities of the markup's own text read.
snapshotText = (s, max = 1500) => {
  const entities = (t) => t.replace(/&(lt|gt|quot|apos|amp|#39|#x27|nbsp);/g, (_, e) => ({ lt: "<", gt: ">", quot: '"', apos: "'", amp: "&", "#39": "'", "#x27": "'", nbsp: " " })[e]).replace(/&#(\d+);/g, (_, n) => String.fromCodePoint(Number(n)));
  return entities(entities(String(s ?? "").replace(/<!\[CDATA\[([\s\S]*?)\]\]>/g, "$1")).replace(/<[^>]*>/g, " ")).replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim().slice(0, max);
}
// %%
// The items of an RSS or Atom feed. No XML parser runs in a Worker; a feed's items are flat, so each field is read by its tag.
snapshotFeed = (xml) => {
  const tag = (s, name) => (new RegExp("<" + name + "(?:\\s[^>]*)?>([\\s\\S]*?)</" + name + ">").exec(s) || [])[1] || "";
  const href = (s) => (/<link\s[^>]*?href="([^"]*)"/.exec(s) || [])[1] || "";
  return String(xml).split(/<(?:item|entry)[\s>]/).slice(1).map((s) => ({
    id: snapshotText(tag(s, "guid") || tag(s, "id"), 500),
    title: snapshotText(tag(s, "title"), 500),
    url: snapshotText(tag(s, "link") || href(s), 2000),
    author: snapshotText(tag(s, "dc:creator") || tag(tag(s, "author"), "name"), 200),
    published: snapshotText(tag(s, "pubDate") || tag(s, "published") || tag(s, "updated"), 100),
    summary: tag(s, "description") || tag(s, "summary") || tag(s, "content") || tag(s, "content:encoded")
  }));
}
// %%
// The items of a JSON answer, each field read at the path the source's map names.
snapshotJson = (data, src) => {
  const at = (o, path) => String(path).split(".").reduce((v, k) => (v == null ? undefined : v[k]), o);
  const list = src.items ? at(data, src.items) : data;
  return (Array.isArray(list) ? list : []).map((o) => Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(src.map || {}).map(([k, p]) => [k, /\{/.test(p) ? String(p).replace(/\{([^}]+)\}/g, (_, q) => at(o, q) ?? "") : at(o, p)])));
}
// %%
// What one source's answer holds, in the kept shape: { of, items }.
snapshotItems = (body, src, now = Date.now()) => {
  const raw = src.kind === "json" ? snapshotJson(JSON.parse(body), src) : snapshotFeed(body);
  const keep = src.keep ? new RegExp(src.keep) : null, since = src.days ? now - src.days * 86400000 : null;
  const items = [];
  for (const r of raw) {
    if (keep && !keep.test(String(r.title) + " " + String(r.summary))) continue;
    const t = r.published ? Date.parse(r.published) : NaN;
    if (since !== null && !(t >= since)) continue;
    const item = { id: String(r.id || r.url || r.title || ""), title: snapshotText(r.title, 500), url: r.url ? String(r.url) : undefined, points: r.points == null ? undefined : Number(r.points), comments: r.comments == null ? undefined : Number(r.comments), author: r.author ? String(r.author) : undefined, published: Number.isFinite(t) ? new Date(t).toISOString() : undefined, discussion: r.discussion ? String(r.discussion) : undefined, summary: snapshotText(r.summary) || undefined, source: src.name, tier: src.tier };
    if (item.id && item.title) items.push(JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(item)));
    if (items.length >= (src.limit || 500)) break;
  }
  return { of: raw.length, items };
}
// %%
// A list of sources as the owner gave it, or the reason it is refused.
snapshotCheck = (list) => {
  if (!Array.isArray(list) || !list.length || list.length > 40) return "sources is a list of 1 to 40";
  const seen = new Set();
  for (const s of list) {
    if (!s || typeof s !== "object" || !/^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,39}$/.test(s.name || "") || seen.has(s.name)) return "each source has its own name of a-z, 0-9 and -";
    seen.add(s.name);
    if (!["research", "blogger", "aggregator"].includes(s.tier)) return s.name + ": tier is research, blogger or aggregator";
    if (!["json", "rss", "atom"].includes(s.kind)) return s.name + ": kind is json, rss or atom";
    try { if (new URL(s.url).protocol !== "https:") throw 0; } catch { return s.name + ": url is an https address"; }
    if (s.kind === "json" && (!s.map || typeof s.map !== "object" || !s.map.title)) return s.name + ": a json source has a map with a title";
    if (s.keep !== undefined) try { new RegExp(s.keep); } catch { return s.name + ": keep is a pattern"; }
  }
  return null;
}
// %%
snapshotOps = {
  const STATIC = "com.lopecode.brain.static.put";
  const dayOf = (now) => new Date(now).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
  const put = async (path, value) => {
    const r = await xrpc.fetch(STATIC, { method: "POST", params: { path, type: "application/json", public: "true", tags: "snapshot" }, body: new TextEncoder().encode(JSON.stringify(value)) });
    return r.ok ? null : "static.put " + r.status;
  };
  const sources = async () => (await rows.get("sources")) || snapshotSources;
  const one = async (src, day, now) => {
    const t = Date.now(), row = { name: src.name, tier: src.tier, status: 0, count: 0, of: 0, bytes: 0, ms: 0, path: null, error: null };
    try {
      const r = await fetch(src.url, { headers: { "user-agent": snapshotAgent, accept: "application/json, application/atom+xml, application/rss+xml, application/xml;q=0.9, */*;q=0.5" } });
      const body = await r.text();
      Object.assign(row, { status: r.status, bytes: body.length });
      if (!r.ok) row.error = "the source answered " + r.status;
      else {
        const { of, items } = snapshotItems(body, src, now);
        Object.assign(row, { of, count: items.length });
        if (items.length) {
          row.path = `snapshot/${day}/${src.name}.json`;
          row.error = await put(row.path, { source: src.name, tier: src.tier, url: src.url, day, fetchedAt: new Date(now).toISOString(), count: items.length, items });
          if (row.error) Object.assign(row, { path: null, count: 0 });
        }
      }
    } catch (e) {
      row.error = String((e && e.message) || e).slice(0, 200);
    }
    row.ms = Date.now() - t;
    return row;
  };
  const run = async (now = Date.now()) => {
    const day = dayOf(now), list = await sources();
    const index = { day, ranAt: new Date(now).toISOString(), sources: await Promise.all(list.map((s) => one(s, day, now))) };
    const items = index.sources.reduce((n, s) => n + s.count, 0);
    await put(`snapshot/${day}/index.json`, index);
    await rows.put("day/" + day, { day, ranAt: index.ranAt, items });
    await put("snapshot/days.json", { days: (await rows.list("day/")).map((r) => r.value).sort((a, b) => (a.day < b.day ? 1 : -1)) });
    log({ at: "snapshot.run", day, items, sources: index.sources.map((s) => `${s.name}:${s.status}:${s.count}`).join(" ") });
    return index;
  };
  // The wrapper ticks once a minute. One run a day, at the first tick after 06:00 UTC.
  let ticked = null;
  const tick = async (now = Date.now()) => {
    const day = dayOf(now);
    if (new Date(now).getUTCHours() < 6 || ticked === day) return false;
    ticked = day;
    if (!(await rows.putIfAbsent("ran/" + day, now))) return false;
    await run(now);
    return true;
  };
  return { run, tick, sources };
}
// %%
snapshot_service = cloudflare.Service(
  "snapshot",
  async (request) => {
    const json = (status, body) => new Response(JSON.stringify(body), { status, headers: { "content-type": "application/json" } });
    const what = new URL(request.url).pathname.split(".").pop();
    if (what === "run") return json(200, await snapshotOps.run());
    if (what === "sources") return json(200, { sources: await snapshotOps.sources(), default: !(await rows.get("sources")) });
    if (what === "setSources") {
      const body = await request.json().catch(() => null);
      if (!body || typeof body !== "object") return json(400, { error: "InvalidRequest", message: "{ sources }" });
      if (body.sources === null) return (await rows.delete("sources")), json(200, { sources: snapshotSources.length, default: true });
      const bad = snapshotCheck(body.sources);
      if (bad) return json(400, { error: "InvalidRequest", message: bad });
      await rows.put("sources", body.sources);
      return json(200, { sources: body.sources.length, default: false });
    }
    return json(404, { error: "MethodNotImplemented", message: "snapshot.run, snapshot.sources and snapshot.setSources" });
  },
  {
    crons: ["0 6 * * *"],
    scheduled: () => snapshotOps.tick(),
    calls: ["com.lopecode.brain.static.put"],
    methods: {
      "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.run": { type: "procedure", allow: "caller.session" },
      "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.sources": { type: "query", who: "anyone" },
      "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.setSources": { type: "procedure", allow: "caller.session" }
    }
  }
)
// %%
snapshot_announce = {
  plugins.add("workers", snapshot_service, { invalidation });
  return "announced snapshot_service";
}
// %%
// The days a Brain has kept, and what one day holds. Reads the public files; no session is needed.
snapshotPanel = ({ base, fetch: send = (...a) => fetch(...a) } = {}) => {
  const muted = "color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)";
  if (!base) return Object.assign(htl.html`<i style=${muted}>Open this on a Brain to see its snapshots.</i>`, { value: null });
  const root = String(base).replace(/\/$/, "") + "/static/snapshot/", box = htl.html`<div></div>`, note = htl.html`<div style=${muted}></div>`;
  const el = Object.assign(htl.html`<div>${box}${note}</div>`, { value: null });
  const get = async (path) => { const r = await send(root + path); return r.ok ? r.json() : null; };
  el.ready = (async () => {
    const days = ((await get("days.json")) || { days: [] }).days;
    if (!days.length) return void box.replaceChildren(htl.html`<i style=${muted}>No snapshot yet.</i>`);
    const pick = Inputs.select(days, { label: "Day", format: (d) => `${d.day}  (${d.items} items)` });
    const table = htl.html`<div></div>`;
    const draw = async () => {
      const index = await get(pick.value.day + "/index.json");
      el.value = index;
      table.replaceChildren(Inputs.table((index ? index.sources : []).map((s) => ({ source: s.name, tier: s.tier, kept: s.count, of: s.of, status: s.status, note: s.error || "", file: s.path ? root.replace(/snapshot\/$/, "") + s.path : "" })), { format: { file: (u) => (u ? htl.html`<a href=${u} target="_blank">json</a>` : "") }, layout: "auto" }));
      note.textContent = index ? `ran ${index.ranAt}` : "";
    };
    pick.addEventListener("input", draw);
    box.replaceChildren(pick, table);
    await draw();
  })();
  return el;
}
// %%
md`## Tests`
// %%
snapshotRig = async ({ feeds = {}, rows = new Map() } = {}) => {
  const files = new Map(), asked = [];
  const sim = await simulate(snapshot_service, {
    rows,
    secrets: { BRAIN_KEY: "k" },
    fetch: async (request) => {
      asked.push({ url: request.url, agent: request.headers.get("user-agent") });
      const f = feeds[request.url];
      if (f === undefined) throw new Error("no route to host");
      return typeof f === "number" ? new Response("refused", { status: f }) : new Response(typeof f === "string" ? f : JSON.stringify(f));
    },
    core: async (request) => {
      const u = new URL(request.url);
      files.set(u.searchParams.get("path"), { public: u.searchParams.get("public"), tags: u.searchParams.get("tags"), caller: request.headers.get("x-brain-caller"), value: JSON.parse(await request.text()) });
      return Response.json({ path: u.searchParams.get("path") });
    }
  });
  const call = async (name, body, caller = "owner") => {
    const r = await sim.fetch("https://snapshot.internal/xrpc/com.lopecode.brain.snapshot." + name, { method: body === undefined ? "GET" : "POST", headers: { "content-type": "application/json", "x-brain-caller": caller }, body: body === undefined ? undefined : JSON.stringify(body) });
    return { status: r.status, data: await r.json() };
  };
  return { sim, files, asked, rows, call };
}
// %%
snapshotFixtures = ({
  rss: `<?xml version="1.0"?><rss><channel><title>Feed</title><link>https://blog.example/</link>
<item><title>A &amp; B: <![CDATA[new <i>results</i>]]></title><link>https://blog.example/a</link><guid isPermaLink="false">a-1</guid><dc:creator>Ada</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>&lt;p&gt;It&amp;#39;s &lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
<item><title>Old post</title><link>https://blog.example/old</link><guid>old-1</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Jan 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate><description>old</description></item>
</channel></rss>`,
  atom: `<?xml version="1.0"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>r/x</title>
<entry><author><name>/u/ada</name></author><content type="html">&lt;div&gt;Body &amp;amp; more&lt;/div&gt;</content><id>t3_1</id><link href="https://www.reddit.com/r/x/comments/1/?a=1&amp;b=2" /><updated>2026-10-09T01:00:00+00:00</updated><published>2026-10-09T01:00:00+00:00</published><title>[D] A thread</title></entry></feed>`
})
// %%
test_a_feed_item_is_read_by_its_tags_with_markup_and_entities_taken_out = {
  const now = Date.parse("2026-10-09T06:00:00Z");
  const rss = snapshotItems(snapshotFixtures.rss, { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", kind: "rss", days: 7 }, now);
  expect(rss).toEqual({ of: 2, items: [{ id: "a-1", title: "A & B: new results", url: "https://blog.example/a", author: "Ada", published: "2026-10-08T16:00:00.000Z", summary: "It's bold .", source: "blog", tier: "blogger" }] });
  // Without `days` the old post is kept as well.
  expect(snapshotItems(snapshotFixtures.rss, { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", kind: "rss" }, now).items.map((i) => i.id)).toEqual(["a-1", "old-1"]);
  const atom = snapshotItems(snapshotFixtures.atom, { name: "reddit-x", tier: "aggregator", kind: "atom" }, now);
  expect(atom.items).toEqual([{ id: "t3_1", title: "[D] A thread", url: "https://www.reddit.com/r/x/comments/1/?a=1&b=2", author: "/u/ada", published: "2026-10-09T01:00:00.000Z", summary: "Body & more", source: "reddit-x", tier: "aggregator" }]);
  // keep, limit, and a summary cut at 1500 characters.
  const many = `<rss>${[1, 2, 3, 4].map((n) => `<item><title>T${n}</title><guid>${n}</guid><description>Announce Type: ${n % 2 ? "new" : "replace"} ${"x".repeat(3000)}</description></item>`).join("")}</rss>`;
  const kept = snapshotItems(many, { name: "arxiv", tier: "research", kind: "rss", keep: "Announce Type: (new|cross)", limit: 1 }, now);
  expect([kept.of, kept.items.map((i) => i.id), kept.items[0].summary.length]).toEqual([4, ["1"], 1500]);
  return "rss, atom, keep, days, limit";
}
// %%
test_a_json_source_is_read_by_the_paths_its_map_names = {
  const hn = snapshotSources.find((s) => s.name === "hn"), hf = snapshotSources.find((s) => s.name === "hf-papers");
  const a = snapshotItems(JSON.stringify({ hits: [{ objectID: "7", title: "Show HN", url: null, points: 12, num_comments: 3, author: "pg", created_at: "2026-10-09T00:00:00Z" }, { objectID: "8" }] }), hn);
  expect(a).toEqual({ of: 2, items: [{ id: "7", title: "Show HN", points: 12, comments: 3, author: "pg", published: "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z", discussion: "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=7", source: "hn", tier: "aggregator" }] });
  const b = snapshotItems(JSON.stringify([{ paper: { id: "2610.1", title: "A paper", upvotes: 5, summary: "An\nabstract" }, numComments: 0, publishedAt: "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z" }]), hf);
  expect(b.items).toEqual([{ id: "2610.1", title: "A paper", url: "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.1", points: 5, comments: 0, published: "2026-10-08T00:00:00.000Z", summary: "An abstract", source: "hf-papers", tier: "research" }]);
  // An answer that is not the list the source names gives nothing.
  expect(snapshotItems("{}", hn)).toEqual({ of: 0, items: [] });
  return "hn, hf-papers";
}
// %%
test_a_run_keeps_one_public_file_a_source_and_a_failed_source_does_not_stop_it = {
  const sources = [
    { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "rss", days: 7 },
    { name: "quiet", tier: "blogger", url: "https://quiet.example/feed", kind: "rss", days: 7 },
    { name: "refused", tier: "aggregator", url: "https://refused.example/top.json", kind: "json", map: { id: "id", title: "title" } },
    { name: "down", tier: "research", url: "https://down.example/feed", kind: "rss" },
    { name: "broken", tier: "research", url: "https://broken.example/x.json", kind: "json", map: { id: "id", title: "title" } }
  ];
  const rig = await snapshotRig({ rows: new Map([["sources", sources]]), feeds: { "https://blog.example/feed": snapshotFixtures.rss.replace(/Thu, 08 Oct 2026 16:00:00 GMT/, new Date().toUTCString()), "https://quiet.example/feed": "<rss></rss>", "https://refused.example/top.json": 403, "https://broken.example/x.json": "<html>" } });
  let out;
  const lines = await logged(async () => void (out = await rig.call("run", {})));
  // The day the Worker read from its clock, which the timer test may be holding.
  const day = out.data.day;
  expect(out.status).toBe(200);
  expect(out.data.sources.map((s) => [s.name, s.status, s.count, s.path, s.error && s.error.slice(0, 22)])).toEqual([
    ["blog", 200, 1, `snapshot/${day}/blog.json`, null], ["quiet", 200, 0, null, null], ["refused", 403, 0, null, "the source answered 40"], ["down", 0, 0, null, "no route to host"], ["broken", 200, 0, null, expect.any(String)]
  ]);
  // One fetch a source. (A browser drops User-Agent from a Request, so the header is not seen under simulate.)
  expect(rig.asked.map((a) => a.url)).toEqual(sources.map((s) => s.url));
  // Only the source with items wrote a file; the index and the list of days are written whatever happened.
  expect([...rig.files.keys()].sort()).toEqual([`snapshot/${day}/blog.json`, `snapshot/${day}/index.json`, "snapshot/days.json"].sort());
  const file = rig.files.get(`snapshot/${day}/blog.json`);
  expect([file.public, file.tags]).toEqual(["true", "snapshot"]);
  expect(file.value).toMatchObject({ source: "blog", tier: "blogger", day, count: 1, items: [{ id: "a-1", source: "blog" }] });
  expect(rig.files.get("snapshot/days.json").value).toEqual({ days: [{ day, ranAt: out.data.ranAt, items: 1 }] });
  // One line a run: names, statuses and counts, nothing a source said.
  expect(lines).toContainEqual({ at: "snapshot.run", day, items: 1, sources: "blog:200:1 quiet:200:0 refused:403:0 down:0:0 broken:200:0", worker: "brain-x-snapshot", ray: "" });
  // A second run the same day writes the same paths again.
  rig.files.clear();
  await rig.call("run", {});
  expect(rig.files.has(`snapshot/${day}/blog.json`)).toBe(true);
  expect(rig.files.get("snapshot/days.json").value.days.length).toBe(1);
  return "5 sources, 1 file";
}
// %%
test_the_timer_runs_once_a_day_after_six = {
  const rig = await snapshotRig({ rows: new Map([["sources", [{ name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "rss" }]]]), feeds: { "https://blog.example/feed": snapshotFixtures.rss } });
  // The Worker reads the clock; the test sets it.
  const clock = Date.now;
  const at = async (iso, sim = rig.sim) => {
    Date.now = () => Date.parse(iso);
    try { await sim.scheduled(); } finally { Date.now = clock; }
    return rig.asked.length;
  };
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T05:59:00Z")).toBe(0);
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T06:00:30Z")).toBe(1);
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T06:01:30Z")).toBe(1);
  expect([...rig.files.keys()]).toContain("snapshot/2026-10-09/blog.json");
  // Another instance of the Worker the same day finds the row and does not run.
  const second = await snapshotRig({ rows: rig.rows, feeds: {} });
  expect(await at("2026-10-09T09:00:00Z", second.sim)).toBe(1);
  expect(second.asked.length).toBe(0);
  expect(await at("2026-10-10T07:00:00Z")).toBe(2);
  return "2 runs in 2 days";
}
// %%
test_the_owner_sets_the_sources_and_a_bad_list_is_refused = {
  const rig = await snapshotRig();
  expect((await rig.call("sources")).data).toEqual({ sources: snapshotSources, default: true });
  const mine = [{ name: "blog", tier: "blogger", url: "https://blog.example/feed", kind: "rss", days: 7 }];
  expect(await rig.call("setSources", { sources: mine })).toEqual({ status: 200, data: { sources: 1, default: false } });
  expect((await rig.call("sources")).data).toEqual({ sources: mine, default: false });
  for (const bad of [[], [{ ...mine[0], name: "Blog" }], [mine[0], mine[0]], [{ ...mine[0], tier: "news" }], [{ ...mine[0], kind: "html" }], [{ ...mine[0], url: "http://blog.example/" }], [{ ...mine[0], kind: "json" }], [{ ...mine[0], keep: "(" }], "x"])
    expect((await rig.call("setSources", { sources: bad })).status).toBe(400);
  expect((await rig.call("setSources", { sources: null })).data).toEqual({ sources: snapshotSources.length, default: true });
  expect((await rig.call("nope", {})).status).toBe(404);
  // The list this module ships is one the check accepts.
  expect(snapshotCheck(snapshotSources)).toBe(null);
  expect(new Set(snapshotSources.map((s) => s.tier))).toEqual(new Set(["research", "blogger", "aggregator"]));
  return snapshotSources.length + " default sources";
}
// %%
test_snapshot_declares_its_rules_its_timer_and_one_call = {
  const { meta } = await snapshot_service.emit();
  expect(meta.worker).toBe("brain-x-snapshot");
  expect([meta.calls, meta.secrets, meta.crons]).toEqual([["com.lopecode.brain.static.put"], [], ["0 6 * * *"]]);
  const N = "com.lopecode.brain.snapshot.";
  const ask = (m, caller, via = "") => decide(meta.access[N + m], { caller: callerOf({ caller, via }), origin: callerOf({ caller, via }), request: { params: {} } }).allow;
  expect([ask("run", "owner", "session"), ask("run", "owner", "token"), ask("run", "token:laptop"), ask("run", "worker:brain-x-echo"), ask("run", "anonymous")]).toEqual([true, false, false, false, false]);
  expect([ask("setSources", "owner", "session"), ask("setSources", "did:plc:friend"), ask("setSources", "anonymous")]).toEqual([true, false, false]);
  expect([ask("sources", "anonymous"), ask("sources", "did:plc:friend")]).toEqual([true, true]);
  return meta.worker;
}
// %%
test_the_panel_lists_the_days_and_the_sources_of_one = {
  const files = {
    "https://b.example/static/snapshot/days.json": { days: [{ day: "2026-10-09", ranAt: "2026-10-09T06:00:10.000Z", items: 3 }] },
    "https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/index.json": { day: "2026-10-09", ranAt: "2026-10-09T06:00:10.000Z", sources: [{ name: "hn", tier: "aggregator", status: 200, count: 3, of: 30, path: "snapshot/2026-10-09/hn.json", error: null }, { name: "blog", tier: "blogger", status: 403, count: 0, of: 0, path: null, error: "the source answered 403" }] }
  };
  const el = snapshotPanel({ base: "https://b.example/", fetch: async (u) => (files[u] ? Response.json(files[u]) : new Response("", { status: 404 })) });
  await el.ready;
  expect(el.value.sources.length).toBe(2);
  expect(el.textContent).toContain("ran 2026-10-09T06:00:10.000Z");
  expect([...el.querySelectorAll("a")].map((a) => a.href)).toEqual(["https://b.example/static/snapshot/2026-10-09/hn.json"]);
  const none = snapshotPanel({ base: "https://b.example/", fetch: async () => new Response("", { status: 404 }) });
  await none.ready;
  expect(none.textContent).toBe("No snapshot yet.");
  expect(snapshotPanel({}).textContent).toBe("Open this on a Brain to see its snapshots.");
  return "2 sources shown";
}
